comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T07:38:03.082Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict 3148-item all-status corpus without omissions and pm-presets sdk_unavailable search found no owner of this specific event. All open GitHub issue comments were inspected. Release-health pm-7zs0 has the initial live failure receipt. GitHub source pm-presets/src/sdk-loader.ts throws SimulationRefusal when none of its supplied anchors resolve @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk. Existing pm-presets PR170 is independently active; no ownership or implementation there is assumed. Intake open/unclaimed."
  "2026-10-29T07:50:40.710Z","harness:codex","Upstream source inspection: pm-presets PR170 head a251c073bef06c90cf9e8400e1b3fafb97a3cf30 now canonicalizes SDK anchors with realpathSync and catches SDK-loading failure in parameterSafeApi, returning the host typed refusal-result contract. This matches the observed earlier development-worktree stack and is promising remediation, but PR170 is still open and its package publication/deployment has not been independently verified here. Retain the unresolved Sentry event and release blocker until that verification; do not bypass the core gate or take over the independently active package PR."
  "2026-10-29T07:53:18.513Z","harness:codex","Independent 2026-10-29 full observability gate completed: Sentry API access succeeds and exactly one high unresolved issue blocks the zero-high threshold, PM-CLI-3Q unexpected_fault. Telemetry independently passes: weighted seven-day finish error rate5.89 percent and zero failure rows missing error codes. CLI telemetry flush drains the local queue to zero bytes. No suppression or gate-threshold change was made."
  "2026-10-29T10:42:41.994Z","harness:codex","At 10:40 UTC the independently progressing pm-presets PR170 is still OPEN and now at 640600bd2df867f670587dda691bfd036de77816, with GitHub mergeStateStatus BLOCKED while its new remote validation runs. Its published PR evidence describes canonical SDK anchors and typed host refusals, but no merged/published remediation has been verified. The current core observability gate still identifies only PM-CLI-3Q as its release blocker; recent real core command spans and delivery pairs pass independently. Retain this open intake and the automated release issue until upstream acceptance and real producer verification."
  "2026-10-29T14:56:21.871Z","harness:codex","Fresh 2026-10-29 14:40-14:46 UTC observability check: Sentry access succeeds with exactly one high blocker PM-CLI-3Q and zero criticals; required telemetry independently passes at5.91 percent finish error rate with zero failures missing error codes. A newly rebuilt core command produced span a188d55d117f01c9; subsequent flush drains1 queued row to0, three recent real context sessions each have1 start and1 finish, and broker ready/unacked counts are0. Upstream pm-presets PR170 remains open at40312d411ed4d308be93e03a22cc8d317a813a28 with no merged receipt and npm2026.10.28. New related host producer/provenance report GH1625 is recorded separately under pm-gh1625; no fault was suppressed or resolved to clear release admission."
  "2026-10-29T16:20:01.256Z","harness:codex","Fresh final-code observability evidence at2026-10-29 16:14-16:18 UTC: Sentry access succeeds with0 criticals and the same sole high blocker PM-CLI-3Q. Required telemetry passes at5.95 percent finish error rate and0 missing error codes. Rebuilt CLI emits pm.command span971dc1f2f06af2be; three recent real context sessions each pair1 start with1 finish, a real flush drains1 queued entry to0, and broker ready/unacked counts are0. Upstream pm-presets PR170 is still open/unmerged at40312d411ed4d308be93e03a22cc8d317a813a28. npm now publishes2026.10.29, but its gitHead650d6565da96f5030c2e20c72cd1bc26c2512990 diverges from the repair branch and the SDK-loader repair remains in the unmerged diff; the version bump does not establish remediation. Release admission remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T17:48:55.768Z","harness:codex","Continuation refresh: the normal required Sentry/telemetry gate still reports0 criticals and1 high release blocker; no suppression or issue resolution was applied. The public2026.10.28 release verifier remains green across npm/npx/Bun/bunx and MCP. Native scheduled and dispatcher runs for2026.10.29 both failed before publication; this is distinct from duplicate automatic cuts. Upstream PR170 remains independently active; no ownership was overridden."
  "2026-10-29T19:55:31.772Z","harness:codex","Fresh required gate2026-10-29: Sentry0 critical/1 high, blocking PM-CLI-3Q as unexpected_fault. Full issue/event verification:2 events, latest03:11:51Z, host2026.10.25, sdk_unavailable. Required telemetry independently passes5.85% with0 missing error-code rows; real recent context span and matched event pairs are visible. Native schedule40845058453 and dispatcher40813895480 both failed before publication today; public core remains2026.10.28. Upstream pm-presets PR170 headb298258843116f5a23dcff63d25e5b986996f97f is still OPEN/BLOCKED with queued required checks. This intake remains open/unclaimed; no duplicate owner or core error suppression, no assertion that upstream fix is published."
  "2026-10-30T19:44:36.160Z","harness:claude-code","2026-10-30 remediation. Root cause reproduced: a standalone pm-presets extension copy (no node_modules) resolves the host SDK through process.argv[1], and a global npm install reaches pm through a bin symlink, so createRequire searched beside the link. Repaired in the owning package by unbraind/pm-presets#181 (squash 1f704ff, pm-presets item pm-jzy6): the invoked entry follows its symlink first, while workspace anchors keep their given location (CodeRabbit finding). pm-presets 2026.10.30 is published as npm latest with gitHead 1f704ff. Installed-consumer verification in an isolated npm prefix with the global bin symlink and the extension node_modules removed: host 2026.10.25 with pm-presets 2026.10.29 makes pm presets simulate exit 1 with sdk_unavailable (the PM-CLI-3Q signature); host 2026.10.25 and host 2026.10.28 with 2026.10.30 exit 0. PM-CLI-3Q was resolved in Sentry with that evidence as a note. The release gate command from release.yml then reported 0 critical, 0 high and no blocking ids. Operator Auto Release run 41117123853 was dispatched on main 5f1540b56 for the 2026.10.30 cut."
close_reason: PM-CLI-3Q is fixed in pm-presets and the daily release shipped through the ordinary gates
